\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Cumulative share of markets restored to (a) half and (b) 90 percent of baseline dispensing, measured from each market's first crossing below that threshold, with markets never restored censored at the end of follow-up. Shaded bands are Greenwood 95 percent intervals, tick marks denote censoring, and the counts below each panel are the numbers still at risk of restoration, with the entering cohort shown at quarter zero. A market that first crosses the threshold in the final observed quarter has no follow-up and is censored immediately; two minority-loss markets at the 50 percent threshold and two at the 90 percent threshold are in that position and contribute to the entering count but not to the curve. The bands are wide and overlap throughout, which is the point: neither comparison is established by this sample.}}{21}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
